    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a PepsiCo route decision engine agent. \n\nImportant: When making tool calls, use actual data values from the incoming webhook, not literal template strings.\n\nYour task:\n1. Use the execute_route tool available to the Logistic MCP Client to execute the chosen option\n2. Use the notify_delivery_delay tool available to the Retail Client to notify the retailer of the delay\n\nFor steps 1 and 2, construct the payload using the incoming webhook data with this structure:\n{\n  \"route_id\": \"{{ $json.body.route_id }}\",\n  \"truck_id\": \"{{ $json.body.truck_id }}\",\n  \"chosen_option\": {\n    \"option_id\": \"{{ $json.body.chosen_option.option_id }}\",\n    \"route_number\": {{ $json.body.chosen_option.route_number }},\n    \"distance_miles\": {{ $json.body.chosen_option.distance_miles }},\n    \"eta_minutes\": {{ $json.body.chosen_option.eta_minutes }}\n  }\n}\n\nDo not include sn_student_id in any tool calls.\n\n3. Use the update_execute_status tool available to the ServiceNow MCP Client to update the status to 'dispatched'\n\nFor step 3, use this payload:\n{\n    \"route_id\": \"{{ $json.body.route_id }}\",\n    \"status\": \"dispatched\"\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
